{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_000bc9e8-798d-5e0e-9c9e-81e67321a1fb",
  "name": "10.1 Powers of products and products of powers",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Powers of products and products of powers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use (ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ and reverse the relationship for common positive integer indices."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In a power aⁿ, a is the base and n is the index. For positive integer n, the notation means n repeated factors of a. A product inside brackets is raised to the same power for each factor: (ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Conversely, if all the factors have the same index, combine their bases: aⁿbⁿ = (ab)ⁿ. The rule applies to multiplication, not addition. A coefficient inside the bracket is also raised to the power."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockMathEquation",
        "attrs": {
          "math_equation": "(ab)^n=a^nb^n"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Expand (3xy)²."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3²x²y² = 9x²y²."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Write 125a³ as a power of a product."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "125=5³, so 125a³=(5a)³."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Independent practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work these out in your notebook before looking at the self-check below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Expand (4p)³."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Combine 16x²y² into one square."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Self-check"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
